t":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-03-01T02:06:42Z","updated_at":"2025-04-18T17:26:14Z","closed_at":"2025-04-18T17:26:14Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4-rc3 and 4.4-rc2\n- Not reproducible in 4.3-stable\n- Likely occurs in every build after 8e6ade8\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.rc3 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6603) - AMD Ryzen 9 7900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen trying to instantiate a large number (20,000+) of child scenes, the game now simply crashes silently in 4.4, with no error displayed in editor.\n\nChecking the logs, this is produced:\n\n```\nERROR: Element limit reached.\n   at: _allocate_rid (./core/templates/rid_owner.h:133)\nERROR: Parameter \"mem\" is null.\n   at: initialize_rid (./core/templates/rid_owner.h:276)\n```\n\nIn 4.3, regardless of the number of child scenes we attempted to spawn (up to 100,000), it worked fine and allowed us to test out performance numbers, but now with 4.4 we simply appear to hit a hard wall and cannot go any higher.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Load MRP\n- Hit play\n- The log for unit count should go up, and then you'll get \"Debugging process stopped\" suddenly.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[RIDRepro.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19034876/RIDRepro.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.